(64, NULL, 'Solesmes', 'Benedic anima (Ps.103 - Textus antiquus)', 0, 'ps', NULL, NULL, 'Andrew Hinkley', '', NULL, '[[\"tex\",\"\\\\grechangedim{linepunctummorashift}{-0.02 cm}{scalable}\\r\\n\\\\gresetclivisalignment{never}\",{}],[\"gabc\",\"(f3) 1. B\\u00e9(e)ne(f)dic,(h) \\u00e1(h)ni(h)ma(h) me(h)a,(h) <b>D\\u00f3</b>(i)mi(hr)no :(h.) *(:) D\\u00f3(h)mi(h)ne,(h) De(h)us(h) me(h)us,(h) ma(h)gni(h)fi(h)c\\u00e1(h)tus(h) es(h) ve(h//)<i>he</i>(g)<b>m\\u00e9n</b>(e fr)ter.(f.) (::) ()<i>Flexa :</i> d{u}x(h) est(h) e(h)\\u00f3(h fr)rum :(f.) +() (h) (h) (h) (::)\",{}],[\"tex\",\"2.~Confessi\\u00f3nem, et dec\\u00f3rem indu{\\\\bf \\u00ed}sti~:~* am\\u00edctus l\\u00famine sicut ve{\\\\it sti}{\\\\bf m\\u00e9n}to~:\\\\\\\\\\r\\n3.~Ext\\u00e9ndens caelum sicut {\\\\bf pel}lem~:~* qui tegis aquis superi\\u00f3{\\\\it ra} {\\\\bf e}jus.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n4.~Qui ponis nubem asc\\u00e9nsum {\\\\bf tu}um~:~* qui \\u00e1mbulas super pennas {\\\\it ven}{\\\\bf t\\u00f3}rum.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n5.~Qui facis \\u00e1ngelos tuos, {\\\\bf sp\\u00ed}ritus~:~* et min\\u00edstros tuos ignem {\\\\it u}{\\\\bf r\\u00e9n}tem.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n6.~Qui fund\\u00e1sti terram super stabilit\\u00e1tem {\\\\bf su}am~:~* non inclin\\u00e1bitur in sa\\u00e9cu{\\\\it lum} {\\\\bf sa\\u00e9}culi.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n7.~Ab\\u00fdssus, sicut vestim\\u00e9ntum, am\\u00edctus {\\\\bf e}jus~:~* super montes sta{\\\\it bunt} {\\\\bf a}quae.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n8.~Ab increpati\\u00f3ne tua {\\\\bf f\\u00fa}gient~:~* a voce ton\\u00edtrui tui for{\\\\it mi}{\\\\bf d\\u00e1}bunt.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n9.~Asc\\u00e9ndunt montes, et desc\\u00e9ndunt {\\\\bf cam}pi~* in locum, quem fund\\u00e1{\\\\it sti} {\\\\bf e}is.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n10.~T\\u00e9rminum posu\\u00edsti, quem non transgredi{\\\\bf \\u00e9n}tur~:~* neque convert\\u00e9ntur oper\\u00ed{\\\\it re} {\\\\bf ter}ram.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n11.~Qui em\\u00edttis fontes in con{\\\\bf v\\u00e1l}libus~:~* inter medium m\\u00f3ntium pertrans\\u00ed{\\\\it bunt} {\\\\bf a}quae.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n12.~Pot\\u00e1bunt omnes b\\u00e9stiae {\\\\bf a}gri~:~* exspect\\u00e1bunt \\u00f3nagri in si{\\\\it ti} {\\\\bf su}a.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n13.~Super ea v\\u00f3lucres caeli habi{\\\\bf t\\u00e1}bunt~:~* de m\\u00e9dio petr\\u00e1rum da{\\\\it bunt} {\\\\bf vo}ces.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n14.~Rigans montes de superi\\u00f3ribus {\\\\bf su}is~:~* de fructu \\u00f3perum tu\\u00f3rum sati\\u00e1bi{\\\\it tur} {\\\\bf ter}ra~:\\\\\\\\\\r\\n15.~Prod\\u00facens fenum ju{\\\\bf m\\u00e9n}tis,~* et herbam servit\\u00fa{\\\\it ti} {\\\\bf h\\u00f3}minum~:\\\\\\\\\\r\\n16.~Ut ed\\u00facas panem de {\\\\bf ter}ra~:~* et vinum laet\\u00edficet {\\\\it cor} {\\\\bf h\\u00f3}minis~:\\\\\\\\\\r\\n17.~Ut exh\\u00edlaret f\\u00e1ciem in {\\\\bf \\u00f3}leo~:~* et panis cor h\\u00f3minis {\\\\it con}{\\\\bf f\\u00edr}met.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n18.~Saturab\\u00fantur ligna campi, et cedri L\\u00edbani, quas plan{\\\\bf t\\u00e1}vit~:~* illic p\\u00e1sseres nidi{\\\\it fi}{\\\\bf c\\u00e1}bunt.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n19.~Her\\u00f3dii domus dux est e\\u00f3rum~:~$\\\\dag$ montes exc\\u00e9lsi {\\\\bf cer}vis~:~* petra ref\\u00fagium he{\\\\it ri}{\\\\bf n\\u00e1}ciis.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n20.~Fecit lunam in {\\\\bf t\\u00e9m}pora~:~* sol cogn\\u00f3vit occ\\u00e1{\\\\it sum} {\\\\bf su}um.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n21.~Posu\\u00edsti t\\u00e9nebras, et facta {\\\\bf est} nox~:~* in ipsa pertrans\\u00edbunt omnes b\\u00e9sti{\\\\it ae} {\\\\bf sil}vae.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n22.~C\\u00e1tuli le\\u00f3num rugi\\u00e9ntes, ut {\\\\bf r\\u00e1}piant,~* et quaerant a Deo e{\\\\it scam} {\\\\bf si}bi.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n23.~Ortus est sol, et congre{\\\\bf g\\u00e1}ti sunt~:~* et in cub\\u00edlibus suis collo{\\\\it ca}{\\\\bf b\\u00fan}tur.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n24.~Ex\\u00edbit homo ad opus {\\\\bf su}um~:~* et ad operati\\u00f3nem suam usque {\\\\it ad} {\\\\bf v\\u00e9}sperum.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n25.~Quam magnific\\u00e1ta sunt \\u00f3pera tua, D\\u00f3mine!~$\\\\dag$ \\u00f3mnia in sapi\\u00e9ntia fe{\\\\bf c\\u00ed}sti~:~* impl\\u00e9ta est terra possessi\\u00f3{\\\\it ne} {\\\\bf tu}a.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n26.~Hoc mare magnum, et spati\\u00f3sum {\\\\bf m\\u00e1}nibus~:~* illic rept\\u00edlia, quorum non {\\\\it est} {\\\\bf n\\u00fa}merus.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n27.~Anim\\u00e1lia pus\\u00edlla cum {\\\\bf ma}gnis~:~* illic naves per{\\\\it trans}{\\\\bf \\u00ed}bunt.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n28.~Draco iste, quem form\\u00e1sti ad illud\\u00e9ndum {\\\\bf e}i~:~* \\u00f3mnia a te exsp\\u00e9ctant ut des illis escam {\\\\it in} {\\\\bf t\\u00e9m}pore.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n29.~Dante te illis, {\\\\bf c\\u00f3l}ligent~:~* aperi\\u00e9nte te manum tuam, \\u00f3mnia impleb\\u00fantur bo{\\\\it ni}{\\\\bf t\\u00e1}te.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n30.~Avert\\u00e9nte autem te f\\u00e1ciem, turbab\\u00fantur~:~$\\\\dag$ \\u00e1uferes sp\\u00edritum e\\u00f3rum, et de{\\\\bf f\\u00ed}cient,~* et in p\\u00falverem suum re{\\\\it ver}{\\\\bf t\\u00e9n}tur.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n31.~Em\\u00edttes sp\\u00edritum tuum, et crea{\\\\bf b\\u00fan}tur~:~* et renov\\u00e1bis f\\u00e1ci{\\\\it em} {\\\\bf ter}rae.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n32.~Sit gl\\u00f3ria D\\u00f3mini in {\\\\bf sa\\u00e9}culum~:~* laet\\u00e1bitur D\\u00f3minus in op\\u00e9ri{\\\\it bus} {\\\\bf su}is~:\\\\\\\\\\r\\n33.~Qui r\\u00e9spicit terram, et facit eam {\\\\bf tr\\u00e9}mere~:~* qui tangit m\\u00f3ntes, {\\\\it et} {\\\\bf f\\u00fa}migant.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n34.~Cant\\u00e1bo D\\u00f3mino in vita {\\\\bf me}a~:~* ps\\u00e1llam Deo meo qu\\u00e1m{\\\\it di}{\\\\bf u} sum.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n35.~Juc\\u00fandum sit ei el\\u00f3quium {\\\\bf me}um~:~* ego vero delect\\u00e1bor {\\\\it in} {\\\\bf D\\u00f3}mino.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n36.~Def\\u00edciant peccat\\u00f3res a terra, et in\\u00edqui ita ut {\\\\bf non} sint~:~* b\\u00e9nedic, \\u00e1nima me{\\\\it a}, {\\\\bf D\\u00f3}mino.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n\\\\\\\\\\r\\n{\\\\it Et repetitur antiphona} D\\u00f3minus Jesus. {\\\\it ut supra.}\",{}]]', NULL, '2.~Confessiónem, et decórem indu{\\bf í}sti~:~* amíctus lúmine sicut ve{\\it sti}{\\bf mén}to~:\\\\\n3.~Exténdens caelum sicut {\\bf pel}lem~:~* qui tegis aquis superió{\\it ra} {\\bf e}jus.\\\\\n4.~Qui ponis nubem ascénsum {\\bf tu}um~:~* qui ámbulas super pennas {\\it ven}{\\bf tó}rum.\\\\\n5.~Qui facis ángelos tuos, {\\bf spí}ritus~:~* et minístros tuos ignem {\\it u}{\\bf rén}tem.\\\\\n6.~Qui fundásti terram super stabilitátem {\\bf su}am~:~* non inclinábitur in saécu{\\it lum} {\\bf saé}culi.\\\\\n7.~Abýssus, sicut vestiméntum, amíctus {\\bf e}jus~:~* super montes sta{\\it bunt} {\\bf a}quae.\\\\\n8.~Ab increpatióne tua {\\bf fú}gient~:~* a voce tonítrui tui for{\\it mi}{\\bf dá}bunt.\\\\\n9.~Ascéndunt montes, et descéndunt {\\bf cam}pi~* in locum, quem fundá{\\it sti} {\\bf e}is.\\\\\n10.~Términum posuísti, quem non transgredi{\\bf én}tur~:~* neque converténtur operí{\\it re} {\\bf ter}ram.\\\\\n11.~Qui emíttis fontes in con{\\bf vál}libus~:~* inter medium móntium pertransí{\\it bunt} {\\bf a}quae.\\\\\n12.~Potábunt omnes béstiae {\\bf a}gri~:~* exspectábunt ónagri in si{\\it ti} {\\bf su}a.\\\\\n13.~Super ea vólucres caeli habi{\\bf tá}bunt~:~* de médio petrárum da{\\it bunt} {\\bf vo}ces.\\\\\n14.~Rigans montes de superióribus {\\bf su}is~:~* de fructu óperum tuórum satiábi{\\it tur} {\\bf ter}ra~:\\\\\n15.~Prodúcens fenum ju{\\bf mén}tis,~* et herbam servitú{\\it ti} {\\bf hó}minum~:\\\\\n16.~Ut edúcas panem de {\\bf ter}ra~:~* et vinum laetíficet {\\it cor} {\\bf hó}minis~:\\\\\n17.~Ut exhílaret fáciem in {\\bf ó}leo~:~* et panis cor hóminis {\\it con}{\\bf fír}met.\\\\\n18.~Saturabúntur ligna campi, et cedri Líbani, quas plan{\\bf tá}vit~:~* illic pásseres nidi{\\it fi}{\\bf cá}bunt.\\\\\n19.~Heródii domus dux est eórum~:~$\\dag$ montes excélsi {\\bf cer}vis~:~* petra refúgium he{\\it ri}{\\bf ná}ciis.\\\\\n20.~Fecit lunam in {\\bf tém}pora~:~* sol cognóvit occá{\\it sum} {\\bf su}um.\\\\\n21.~Posuísti ténebras, et facta {\\bf est} nox~:~* in ipsa pertransíbunt omnes bésti{\\it ae} {\\bf sil}vae.\\\\\n22.~Cátuli leónum rugiéntes, ut {\\bf rá}piant,~* et quaerant a Deo e{\\it scam} {\\bf si}bi.\\\\\n23.~Ortus est sol, et congre{\\bf gá}ti sunt~:~* et in cubílibus suis collo{\\it ca}{\\bf bún}tur.\\\\\n24.~Exíbit homo ad opus {\\bf su}um~:~* et ad operatiónem suam usque {\\it ad} {\\bf vé}sperum.\\\\\n25.~Quam magnificáta sunt ópera tua, Dómine!~$\\dag$ ómnia in sapiéntia fe{\\bf cí}sti~:~* impléta est terra possessió{\\it ne} {\\bf tu}a.\\\\\n26.~Hoc mare magnum, et spatiósum {\\bf má}nibus~:~* illic reptília, quorum non {\\it est} {\\bf nú}merus.\\\\\n27.~Animália pusílla cum {\\bf ma}gnis~:~* illic naves per{\\it trans}{\\bf í}bunt.\\\\\n28.~Draco iste, quem formásti ad illudéndum {\\bf e}i~:~* ómnia a te exspéctant ut des illis escam {\\it in} {\\bf tém}pore.\\\\\n29.~Dante te illis, {\\bf cól}ligent~:~* aperiénte te manum tuam, ómnia implebúntur bo{\\it ni}{\\bf tá}te.\\\\\n30.~Averténte autem te fáciem, turbabúntur~:~$\\dag$ áuferes spíritum eórum, et de{\\bf fí}cient,~* et in púlverem suum re{\\it ver}{\\bf tén}tur.\\\\\n31.~Emíttes spíritum tuum, et crea{\\bf bún}tur~:~* et renovábis fáci{\\it em} {\\bf ter}rae.\\\\\n32.~Sit glória Dómini in {\\bf saé}culum~:~* laetábitur Dóminus in opéri{\\it bus} {\\bf su}is~:\\\\\n33.~Qui réspicit terram, et facit eam {\\bf tré}mere~:~* qui tangit móntes, {\\it et} {\\bf fú}migant.\\\\\n34.~Cantábo Dómino in vita {\\bf me}a~:~* psállam Deo meo quám{\\it di}{\\bf u} sum.\\\\\n35.~Jucúndum sit ei elóquium {\\bf me}um~:~* ego vero delectábor {\\it in} {\\bf Dó}mino.\\\\\n36.~Defíciant peccatóres a terra, et iníqui ita ut {\\bf non} sint~:~* bénedic, ánima me{\\it a}, {\\bf Dó}mino.\\\\\n\\\\\n{\\it Et repetitur antiphona} Dóminus Jesus. {\\it ut supra.}', NULL, 0, NULL),
