(446, NULL, 'Solesmes', 'Oportebat pati Christum', 1, 'al', '4', NULL, 'Andrew Hinkley', '', NULL, '[[\"tex\",\"\\\\grechangedim{linepunctummorashift}{-0.02 cm}{scalable}\\r\\n\\\\gresetclivisalignment{never}\",{}],[\"gabc\",\"(f3) AL(g)le(fgF\'Efef)l\\u00fa(eg~){ia}.(g.) *(;) (hfg/fge./fefghg.) (,) (hfg/fge./fefghg.) (;) (fjjijvIHivHG.) (,) (fjjijvIHivHG.) (,) (gh!ivviv\'1HF\'Effg.) (::) <sp>V/</sp>. O(g)por(fgF\'Efef/eg)t\\u00e9(ghhg)bat(g.) (,) pa(gh/ihiggfhvGF)ti(eg) Chri(ghhg)stum,(g.) (;) et(g) re(gf)s\\u00far(g)ge(fe)re(fvEDC.) (,) a(e) m\\u00f3r(eg!hvGFgvFE)tu(fg)is,(g.) (:) et(eg) i(g_[oh:h]i_[oh:h]h\'_[oh:h]/ij\'IG)ta(giHG.) (,) in(eg~)tr\\u00e1(g./hfg/fge./fefghG\'Fg)re(g.) (;) in(eg~) gl\\u00f3(g_[oh:h]i_[oh:h]h\'_[oh:h]/ij\'IGivHG)ri(fg)am(fe) *() su(eg)am.(g./hfg/fge./fefghg.) (,) (hfg/fge./fefghg.) (;) (fjjijvIHivHG.) (,) (fjjijvIHivHG.) (,) (gh!ivviv\'1HF\'Effg.) (::)\",{}]]', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
(447, NULL, 'Solesmes', 'Deus Deus meus (Ps. 21 - Textus antiquus)', 0, 'ps', NULL, NULL, 'Andrew Hinkley', '', NULL, '[[\"tex\",\"\\\\grechangedim{linepunctummorashift}{-0.02 cm}{scalable}\\r\\n\\\\gresetclivisalignment{never}\",{}],[\"gabc\",\"(f3) 1. De(h)us,(h) De(h)us(h) me(h)us,(h) r\\u00e9(h)spi(h)ce(h) in(h fr) me : \\u2020(f.) (,) qua(h)re(h) me(h) de(h)<i>re</i>(g[alt:2])<i>li</i>(f[alt:1])<b>qu\\u00ed</b>(hr1 hr)sti?(h.) *(:) lon(h)ge(h) a(h) sa(h)l\\u00fa(h)te(h) me(h)a(h) ver(h)ba(h) de(h)li(h)ct\\u00f3(h)rum(h) me(h)<b>\\u00f3</b>(hr1 fr)rum.(f.) (::)\\r\\n() <i>Flexa :</i> {e}x(h) \\u00fa(h)te(fr)ro : \\u2020(f.) (h) (h) (h)\",{}],[\"tex\",\"2.~Deus meus, clam\\u00e1bo per diem, et {\\\\it non ex}{\\\\bf \\u00e1u}dies : * et nocte, et non ad insipi\\u00e9ntiam {\\\\bf mi}hi.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n3.~Tu autem in {\\\\it sancto} {\\\\bf h\\u00e1}bitas, * laus {\\\\bf Is}ra\\\\\\\"{e}l.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n4.~In te sperav\\u00e9runt {\\\\it patres} {\\\\bf no}stri : * sperav\\u00e9runt, et liber\\u00e1sti {\\\\bf e}os.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n5.~Ad te clamav\\u00e9runt, et {\\\\it salvi} {\\\\bf fa}cti sunt : * in te sperav\\u00e9runt, et non sunt con{\\\\bf f\\u00fa}si.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n6.~Ego autem sum vermis, {\\\\it et non} {\\\\bf ho}mo : * oppr\\u00f3brium h\\u00f3minum, et abj\\u00e9ctio {\\\\bf ple}bis.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n7.~Omnes vid\\u00e9ntes me, {\\\\it deri}{\\\\bf s\\u00e9}runt me : * loc\\u00fati sunt l\\u00e1biis, et mov\\u00e9runt {\\\\bf ca}put.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n8.~Sper\\u00e1vit in D\\u00f3mino, er\\u00ed{\\\\it piat} {\\\\bf e}um : * salvum f\\u00e1ciat eum, qu\\u00f3niam vult {\\\\bf e}um.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n9.~Qu\\u00f3niam tu es, qui extrax\\u00edsti {\\\\it me de} {\\\\bf ven}tre : * spes mea ab ub\\u00e9ribus matris {\\\\bf me}ae.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n10.~In te proj\\u00e9ctus sum ex \\u00fatero : $\\\\dag$ de ventre matris meae Deus {\\\\it meus} {\\\\bf es} tu, * ne disc\\u00e9sseris {\\\\bf a} me :\\\\\\\\\\r\\n11.~Qu\\u00f3niam tribul\\u00e1tio {\\\\it pr\\u00f3xi}{\\\\bf ma} est : * qu\\u00f3niam non est qui {\\\\bf \\u00e1d}juvet.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n12.~Circumded\\u00e9runt me v\\u00ed{\\\\it tuli} {\\\\bf mul}ti : * tauri pingues obse{\\\\bf d\\u00e9}runt me.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n13.~Aperu\\u00e9runt super {\\\\it me os} {\\\\bf su}um, * sicut leo r\\u00e1piens et {\\\\bf r\\u00fa}giens.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n14.~Sicut a{\\\\it qua ef}{\\\\bf f\\u00fa}sus sum : * et disp\\u00e9rsa sunt \\u00f3mnia ossa {\\\\bf me}a.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n15.~Factum est cor meum tamquam ce{\\\\it ra li}{\\\\bf qu\\u00e9}scens * in m\\u00e9dio ventris {\\\\bf me}i.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n16.~Aruit tamquam testa virtus mea, $\\\\dag$ et lingua mea adha\\u00e9sit f\\u00e1u{\\\\it cibus} {\\\\bf me}is : * et in p\\u00falverem mortis dedu{\\\\bf x\\u00ed}sti me.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n17.~Qu\\u00f3niam circumded\\u00e9runt me {\\\\it canes} {\\\\bf mul}ti : * conc\\u00edlium malign\\u00e1ntium ob{\\\\bf s\\u00e9}dit me.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n\\\\hyphenation{\\u00f3-mni-a}\\r\\n18.~Fod\\u00e9runt manus meas et {\\\\it pedes} {\\\\bf me}os : * dinumerav\\u00e9runt \\u00f3mnia ossa {\\\\bf me}a.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n19.~Ipsi vero cons\\u00edderav\\u00e9runt et inspex\\u00e9runt me : $\\\\dag$ divis\\u00e9runt sibi vesti{\\\\it m\\u00e9nta} {\\\\bf me}a, * et super vestem meam mis\\u00e9runt {\\\\bf sor}tem.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n20.~Tu autem, D\\u00f3mine, ne elong\\u00e1veris aux\\u00edlium {\\\\it tuum} {\\\\bf a} me : * ad defensi\\u00f3nem meam {\\\\bf c\\u00f3n}spice.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n21.~Erue a fr\\u00e1mea, Deus, \\u00e1{\\\\it nimam} {\\\\bf me}am : * et de manu canis \\u00fanicam {\\\\bf me}am.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n22.~Salva me ex o{\\\\it re le}{\\\\bf \\u00f3}nis : * et a c\\u00f3rnibus unic\\u00f3rnium humilit\\u00e1tem {\\\\bf me}am.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n23.~Narr\\u00e1bo nomen tuum fr\\u00e1{\\\\it tribus} {\\\\bf me}is : * in m\\u00e9dio eccl\\u00e9siae lau{\\\\bf d\\u00e1}bo te.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n24.~Qui tim\\u00e9bis D\\u00f3minum, lau{\\\\it d\\u00e1te} {\\\\bf e}um : * univ\\u00e9rsum semen Jacob, glorific\\u00e1te {\\\\bf e}um.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n25.~T\\u00edmeat eum omne {\\\\it semen} {\\\\bf Is}ra\\\\\\\"{e}l : * qu\\u00f3niam non sprevit, neque desp\\u00e9xit deprecati\\u00f3nem {\\\\bf p\\u00e1u}peris.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n26.~Nec av\\u00e9rtit f\\u00e1ciem {\\\\it suam} {\\\\bf a} me : * et cum clam\\u00e1rem ad eum, exau{\\\\bf d\\u00ed}vit me.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n27.~Apud te laus mea in eccl\\u00e9{\\\\it sia} {\\\\bf ma}gna : * vota mea reddam in consp\\u00e9ctu tim\\u00e9ntium {\\\\bf e}um.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n28.~Edent p\\u00e1uperes, et saturab\\u00fantur : $\\\\dag$ et laud\\u00e1bunt D\\u00f3minum, qui re{\\\\it qu\\u00edrunt} {\\\\bf e}um : * vivent corda e\\u00f3rum in sa\\u00e9culum {\\\\bf sa\\u00e9}culi.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n29.~Reminisc\\u00e9ntur et convert\\u00e9n{\\\\it tur ad} {\\\\bf D\\u00f3}minum * univ\\u00e9rsi fines {\\\\bf ter}rae.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n30.~Et ador\\u00e1bunt in con{\\\\it sp\\u00e9ctu} {\\\\bf e}jus * univ\\u00e9rsae fam\\u00edliae {\\\\bf g\\u00e9n}tium.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n31.~Qu\\u00f3niam D\\u00f3mi{\\\\it ni est} {\\\\bf re}gnum : * et ipse domin\\u00e1bitur {\\\\bf g\\u00e9n}tium.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n32.~Manducav\\u00e9runt et adorav\\u00e9runt omnes {\\\\it pingues} {\\\\bf ter}rae : * in consp\\u00e9ctu ejus cadent omnes qui desc\\u00e9ndunt in {\\\\bf ter}ram.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n33.~Et \\u00e1nima mea {\\\\it illi} {\\\\bf vi}vet : * et semen meum s\\u00e9rviet {\\\\bf i}psi.\\\\\\\\\\r\\n34.~Annunti\\u00e1bitur D\\u00f3mino gener\\u00e1tio vent\\u00fara : $\\\\dag$ et annunti\\u00e1bunt caeli just\\u00edtiam ejus p\\u00f3pulo {\\\\it qui na}{\\\\bf sc\\u00e9}tur, * quem fecit {\\\\bf D\\u00f3}minus.\",{}]]', NULL, '2.~Deus meus, clamábo per diem, et {\\it non ex}{\\bf áu}dies : * et nocte, et non ad insipiéntiam {\\bf mi}hi.\\\\\n3.~Tu autem in {\\it sancto} {\\bf há}bitas, * laus {\\bf Is}ra\\\"{e}l.\\\\\n4.~In te speravérunt {\\it patres} {\\bf no}stri : * speravérunt, et liberásti {\\bf e}os.\\\\\n5.~Ad te clamavérunt, et {\\it salvi} {\\bf fa}cti sunt : * in te speravérunt, et non sunt con{\\bf fú}si.\\\\\n6.~Ego autem sum vermis, {\\it et non} {\\bf ho}mo : * oppróbrium hóminum, et abjéctio {\\bf ple}bis.\\\\\n7.~Omnes vidéntes me, {\\it deri}{\\bf sé}runt me : * locúti sunt lábiis, et movérunt {\\bf ca}put.\\\\\n8.~Sperávit in Dómino, erí{\\it piat} {\\bf e}um : * salvum fáciat eum, quóniam vult {\\bf e}um.\\\\\n9.~Quóniam tu es, qui extraxísti {\\it me de} {\\bf ven}tre : * spes mea ab ubéribus matris {\\bf me}ae.\\\\\n10.~In te projéctus sum ex útero : $\\dag$ de ventre matris meae Deus {\\it meus} {\\bf es} tu, * ne discésseris {\\bf a} me :\\\\\n11.~Quóniam tribulátio {\\it próxi}{\\bf ma} est : * quóniam non est qui {\\bf ád}juvet.\\\\\n12.~Circumdedérunt me ví{\\it tuli} {\\bf mul}ti : * tauri pingues obse{\\bf dé}runt me.\\\\\n13.~Aperuérunt super {\\it me os} {\\bf su}um, * sicut leo rápiens et {\\bf rú}giens.\\\\\n14.~Sicut a{\\it qua ef}{\\bf fú}sus sum : * et dispérsa sunt ómnia ossa {\\bf me}a.\\\\\n15.~Factum est cor meum tamquam ce{\\it ra li}{\\bf qué}scens * in médio ventris {\\bf me}i.\\\\\n16.~Aruit tamquam testa virtus mea, $\\dag$ et lingua mea adhaésit fáu{\\it cibus} {\\bf me}is : * et in púlverem mortis dedu{\\bf xí}sti me.\\\\\n17.~Quóniam circumdedérunt me {\\it canes} {\\bf mul}ti : * concílium malignántium ob{\\bf sé}dit me.\\\\\n\\hyphenation{ó-mni-a}\n18.~Fodérunt manus meas et {\\it pedes} {\\bf me}os : * dinumeravérunt ómnia ossa {\\bf me}a.\\\\\n19.~Ipsi vero consíderavérunt et inspexérunt me : $\\dag$ divisérunt sibi vesti{\\it ménta} {\\bf me}a, * et super vestem meam misérunt {\\bf sor}tem.\\\\\n20.~Tu autem, Dómine, ne elongáveris auxílium {\\it tuum} {\\bf a} me : * ad defensiónem meam {\\bf cón}spice.\\\\\n21.~Erue a frámea, Deus, á{\\it nimam} {\\bf me}am : * et de manu canis únicam {\\bf me}am.\\\\\n22.~Salva me ex o{\\it re le}{\\bf ó}nis : * et a córnibus unicórnium humilitátem {\\bf me}am.\\\\\n23.~Narrábo nomen tuum frá{\\it tribus} {\\bf me}is : * in médio ecclésiae lau{\\bf dá}bo te.\\\\\n24.~Qui timébis Dóminum, lau{\\it dáte} {\\bf e}um : * univérsum semen Jacob, glorificáte {\\bf e}um.\\\\\n25.~Tímeat eum omne {\\it semen} {\\bf Is}ra\\\"{e}l : * quóniam non sprevit, neque despéxit deprecatiónem {\\bf páu}peris.\\\\\n26.~Nec avértit fáciem {\\it suam} {\\bf a} me : * et cum clamárem ad eum, exau{\\bf dí}vit me.\\\\\n27.~Apud te laus mea in ecclé{\\it sia} {\\bf ma}gna : * vota mea reddam in conspéctu timéntium {\\bf e}um.\\\\\n28.~Edent páuperes, et saturabúntur : $\\dag$ et laudábunt Dóminum, qui re{\\it quírunt} {\\bf e}um : * vivent corda eórum in saéculum {\\bf saé}culi.\\\\\n29.~Reminiscéntur et convertén{\\it tur ad} {\\bf Dó}minum * univérsi fines {\\bf ter}rae.\\\\\n30.~Et adorábunt in con{\\it spéctu} {\\bf e}jus * univérsae famíliae {\\bf gén}tium.\\\\\n31.~Quóniam Dómi{\\it ni est} {\\bf re}gnum : * et ipse dominábitur {\\bf gén}tium.\\\\\n32.~Manducavérunt et adoravérunt omnes {\\it pingues} {\\bf ter}rae : * in conspéctu ejus cadent omnes qui descéndunt in {\\bf ter}ram.\\\\\n33.~Et ánima mea {\\it illi} {\\bf vi}vet : * et semen meum sérviet {\\bf i}psi.\\\\\n34.~Annuntiábitur Dómino generátio ventúra : $\\dag$ et annuntiábunt caeli justítiam ejus pópulo {\\it qui na}{\\bf scé}tur, * quem fecit {\\bf Dó}minus.', NULL, 0, NULL),
