(3948, NULL, 'Vatican', 'Beata es Virgo', 1, 'of', '8', NULL, 'Andrew Hinkley', NULL, NULL, '\"(c4) BE(fg)\\u00c1(g/hjHGgf)TA(ghg) es,(g) *(,) Vir(jvIHkj//ijh/ig/hi/jg , jvIHkj//ijh/ig/hi/jg , ggghvGFgd//gjhi)go(hg) (,) Ma(ig/h!jjk)r\\u00ed(hg)a,(gd) (;) quae(d) \\u00f3(d)mni(d)um(d) por(d)t\\u00e1(dc/d!ff/gh/jg)sti(g) (;) Cre(h)a(g)t\\u00f3(gjIGhh//fh!jvGFfd/ef!ghg)rem:(g) (:) ge(gd)nu(fe)\\u00ed(fhg)sti(g) (,) qui(g) te(gh) fe(hg/hiHGjg//hiHG//fg/hg/hjjh/ig)cit,(g) (:) et(hvGF) in(hji) ae(jhj)t\\u00e9r(hjg)num(gfh) (,) p\\u00e9r(gj)ma(ji)nes(jkJH//gi hjIH//g!jj/hig) Vir(ghg)go,(g) (:) al(gkik~)le(kv//jkjkvJIG//hj/ijHG,hkik//jkjkvJIG//hi//hjg)l\\u00fa(ghg)ia.(g) (::)\"', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL),
(3949, 'g00397', 'Vatican', 'Stetit Angelus (Off)', 1, 'of', '1', NULL, 'Andrew Hinkley', NULL, NULL, '\"(c4) STE(fffvDCdff/hgh)TIT(fgf) *(,) An(f!gh)ge(h)lus(ixhf/hig/ff/ded) (;) jux(d)ta(dgfg) a(dgf/efd/ed)ram(dcd~) tem(dv//c!df/ef!hvGEfd)pli,(d) (:) ha(ixdf!hv//jhivGEfg)bens(f) (,) thu(de)r\\u00ed(gh)bu(hggvEDCd)lum(d) (,) \\u00e1u(c!df/ef!gvEDfv//efd/ed)re(cd)um(dfddc) (,) in(da~) ma(cd)nu(d) su(dfd)a:(d) (:) et(cd~) da(d)ta(fde) sunt(dec) e(c!df/efd)i(d) (,) in(da~)c\\u00e9n(cd~)sa(d) mul(dfd)ta:(d) (:) et(c) a(d)sc\\u00e9n(ixdh//jjh//gih/ig//f!gh/jjg,fhgh//fh!jvGFfdf eg/hjh/jhhgh~)dit(f) (;) fu(ef!gvEDfv//efd)mus(dfddc) a(c!df/e!fg)r\\u00f3(ed/fe)ma(ded)tum(d) (,) in(da~) con(cd~)sp\\u00e9(d)ctu(d) De(ded)i,(d) (:) al(cd)le(fgfhv//ghFD cd/fef/ge,hg/efd//fvEDed)l\\u00fa(cd~)ia.(d) (::)\"', NULL, NULL, 'This Offertory is used for the Feast of St. Michael 29th September. It is also used for the Feasts of St. Gabriel (24th March) and St. Raphael (24th October) without the final Alleluia, except during Paschaltide, according to the 1962 Missale Romanum. The 1961 Graduale Romanum states \"sine Alleluia in Quadrag.\" but does not mention the omission for 24 October. The editions of the Liber Usualis from the 1950s and 1960s state \"sine Alleluia\" for 24 March but make no mention of the omission for 24 October.', 0, NULL),
