(8149, NULL, 'Solesmes 1961', 'Magnificat, 8G 8G* 8c', 0, 'ca', '8', 'G, G*, c', 'Christopher Tatum', NULL, NULL, '\"(c4) 1. Ma(g)gn\\u00ed(hg)fi(gj)cat(j.) *(:) \\u00e1(j)ni(j)ma(j) <i>me</i>(i)<i>a</i>(j) <b>D\\u00f3</b>(h)mi(gr)num.<alt>G</alt>(g.) (::) <i>or :</i>() <b>D\\u00f3</b>(h)mi(gr)num.<alt>G*</alt>(gh..) (::) <i>or :</i>() <i>me</i>(h)<i>a</i>(j) <b>D\\u00f3</b>(k)mi(jr)num.<alt>c</alt>(j.) (::)\\r\\n2. Et(g) ex(h)sul(j)t\\u00e1(j)vit(j) sp\\u00ed(j)ri(j)tus(j) <b>me</b>(k jr)us(j.) *(:) in(j) De(j)o(j) sa(j)lu(j)<i>t\\u00e1</i>(i)<i>ri</i>(j) <b>me</b>(h gr)o.<alt>G</alt>(g.) (::)\"', NULL, '{\\begin{flushleft}\\ \\ 3.\\ Quia respéxit humilitátem ancíllae {\\bf su}ae : * ecce enim ex hoc beátam me dicent omnes gene{\\it rati}{\\bf ó}nes. \\\\\n\\ \\ 4.\\ Quia fecit mihi magna qui {\\bf po}tens est : * et sanctum {\\it nomen} {\\bf e}jus. \\\\\n\\ \\ 5.\\ Et misericórdia ejus a progénie in pro{\\bf gé}nies * timén{\\it tibus} {\\bf e}um. \\\\\n\\ \\ 6.\\ Fecit poténtiam in bráchio {\\bf su}o : * dispérsit supérbos mente {\\it cordis} {\\bf su}i. \\\\\n\\ \\ 7.\\ Depósuit poténtes de {\\bf se}de, * et exal{\\it távit} {\\bf hú}miles. \\\\\n\\ \\ 8.\\ Esuriéntes implévit {\\bf bo}nis : * et dívites dimí{\\it sit in}{\\bf á}nes. \\\\\n\\ \\ 9.\\ Suscépit Israel púerum {\\bf su}um, * recordátus misericór{\\it diae} {\\bf su}ae. \\\\\n\\ \\ 10.\\ Sicut locútus est ad patres {\\bf no}stros, * Abraham et sémini e{\\it jus in} {\\bf saé}cula. \\\\\n\\ \\ 11.\\ Glória Patri, et {\\bf Fí}lio, * et Spirí{\\it tui} {\\bf San}cto. \\\\\n\\ \\ 12.\\ Sicut erat in princípio, et nunc, et {\\bf sem}per, * et in saécula saecu{\\it lórum}. {\\bf A}men.\\end{flushleft}}', '', 0, NULL),
